      "writtenOn": "2024-11-20T16:23:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is ignored I believe (this is the current behaviour).\n\nI don\u0027t think this is possible to write in WGSL, since you cannot write `-\u003e void` for a return, thus you cannot decorate the return.\n\nSo I think the only way it can occur is via writing IR. When creating the IR I know voids are inserted where they are implicitly in the original WGSL.\n\nMy intuition is that annotating a void value is never intentionally done in Tint, so if it occurs that is a programming error, so this should changed to ICE\u0027ing if there is ever an annotation on a void. Does that seem reasonable?\n\nI am going to make that change and confirm that it doesn\u0027t cause any crashes in the tests.",
      "parentUuid": "64d707e2_d371bbc8",
